WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.160
They alternated whose name came first on the papers, to signal that the work was

2
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.820
exactly equal. Stanford Moore and William Stein argued every sentence until a

3
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.180
finding was vetted to perfection, and a colleague described them as a single

4
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.480
intellectual entity.

5
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:25.670
Their automated analyzer used synthetic resins to separate the amino acids, then

6
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:30.470
detected each one through a color-changing ninhydrin reaction, and that machine

7
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:37.950
decoded ribonuclease, an enzyme of 124 amino acids the first enzyme read end to end.

8
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:43.223
Moore compared a protein's sequence to a coded message that dictates the three

9
00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:47.683
-dimensional shape and function of the biological machine, and now they could read

10
00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:48.667
it.

11
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:52.307
Then the bodies of both men failed them and neither stopped.

12
00:00:52.987 --> 00:00:57.187
Guillain-Barre left Stein quadriplegic; he kept guiding his lab and editing

13
00:00:57.187 --> 00:01:01.187
manuscripts with gracious detail, hosting seminars from his apartment.

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.680
ALS took Moore's hands the same hands that once machined solenoid valves and tuned

15
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.020
gear-driven turntables now resting in his lap with an unwilling stillness while in

16
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.440
the lab a pen recorder traced peaks of a molecular logic he could no longer

17
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.680
physically touch. He lived by his own quiet mantra: the investigator does not

18
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.340
usually move from discovery to discovery; he moves from problem to problem.
